WEBVTT

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:54.510
Give these a try.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.120
There's nothing wrong with my eyes.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.280
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:01.850
Hey!

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.500
My eyes are fine...

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.540
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:38.270
...the instant I look away.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.410
I just kept counting...

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:48.850
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:56.220
...that I'd vomited up.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:02.160
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.270
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:13.130
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.180
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:25.850
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:33.680
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.570
I'd ask if you want to come up for a bit, but, you know...

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.010
I'm home.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.840
Oh, welcome back.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.580
Looks like you straightened up the living room, too.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:16.780
Oh, yeah.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.780
You're a bit of a neat freak, I see.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:25.190
I don't enjoy it or anything... It's more like a habit.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.250
Cleaning was one of my chores back at the convent.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.170
Pretty good.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.070
You really captured the feel of it.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.110
I always wondered what it was that you were painting.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:55.410
Me, too.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.520
I've been curious about you, too.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.120
Since I see you here every morning.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:06.950
Oh, I just stop by to pray.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.930
Pray? You believe in God?

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.400
It's just out of habit.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.900
I believe in Him.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:24.140
He was the one who brought me into such a beautiful world.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:30.350
That's why I'm preserving it. I'm preserving the world in all its beauty.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.820
I'm Sayoko.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.420
Oh, I'm Robin.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:42.020
Robin... What a beautiful name.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.480
Robin.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.380
Yes?

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.540
I have a message from Amon.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.280
He said to memorize the contents of this file.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.690
File?

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.850
These are reports from unsolved crimes.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.460
It has case summaries covering the past two years.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:15.100
They all have a 50% chance or less of a witch being the culprit.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:22.430
Anyway, simply seeing the results of the initial investigations should be informative.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.710
Where's Amon?

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.680
He's out with Sakaki.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.140
With Sakaki?

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.880
I still think he should have taken you with him.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.780
Really! Robin was originally supposed to be his partner.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:41.990
What about the job you were originally supposed to be doing, Dojima?!

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:45.830
W-What are you talking about? That's so rude!

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.690
Can't you see that I'm hard at work on it right now?!

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.800
What are those magazines on your desk, then?

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.500
These might look like fashion magazines to you, Chief,

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:56.470
but they're reference material for a case!

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:59.670
What, you don't believe me?!

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:19.160
They're all pretty horrible, aren't they?

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.550
The killer's either a human or a witch...

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:26.900
There are humans beings out there who are worse than witches.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:43.290
Oh, that one. The Yotsuga Pond Park serial murders.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.880
Three victims. No link was ever found in age, occupation, and so on.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:53.450
The only similarity was that the cause of death in each was blood loss from external injuries.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:58.900
Dozens of lacerations all over the body, and they never determined what made them.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.960
How they were killed and the conditions that led to their murder are still unknown.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:08.230
I walk through this park every morning when I go to pray...

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:09.540
No kidding...

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.010
I had no idea that something like this had happened there...

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.250
Why would you?

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:21.590
These murders happened four months before you got here.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:33.160
The killer might still be in the area.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:37.240
A witch, or a sociopath...

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.870
Why don't we go take a look at the scene?

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.210
Maybe we'll find something.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:48.050
Sure.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:52.380
But let's have lunch first. It's a little late, I know.

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:22.510
Thank you.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.000
You can read me, right?

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:46.100
You know what I'm thinking right now.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:47.770
Maybe.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.600
Please try to do it.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.680
Read my mind.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:14.360
Amon...

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:17.500
Partner...

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.300
Abandonment...

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.180
Why does this always happen?

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.780
Amazing! You're right!

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:32.550
You can see into people's minds!

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:40.920
I didn't use my powers.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:46.220
I can see that much even without using powers.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:56.340
Besides, all I can read is intense feelings in things.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.850
I can't see into other people's minds.

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.520
Even though you're S-class?

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:07.510
Oh, so even Craft Users are obsessed with power classes?

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:09.520
I'm not obsessed or anything...

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.020
You're A-class, right?

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:20.190
You could be S-class if you could manage to be more accurate with your power.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.500
Why can't you hit anything?

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:26.270
Beats me.

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:19.520
Here.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:20.690
Thanks.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.010
We'd be in big trouble if the Chief found us right now.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.350
Would you like to drop by my place on the way back?

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:51.760
It's close by, and I'd like to talk some more.

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:57.360
Well, it's taboo for employees to hang out with each other outside of work.

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:00.100
That doesn't matter.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:05.810
That might be nice.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:14.780
It's so peaceful...

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:18.480
It's hard to believe that something like those murders happened here.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:23.580
And the media made such a fuss back then... They're so coldhearted.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:28.490
After just four months, it's as if it never happened.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.250
Someone you know?

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.580
No, I've only talked to her once.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:01.990
Well, that was a waste of time...

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.460
My legs feel like lead...

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.690
If you're looking for Robin, she went out.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.640
She went to go check out Yotsuga Pond Park with Miss Karasuma.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.810
Yotsuga Pond Park? Isn't that where...

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.010
Mr. Amon?

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:39.560
Just as I thought, there's nothing here.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:43.630
Well, the police went over the area with a fine-toothed comb, so it's no surprise.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.740
What do you think, Karasuma?

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:49.200
Is the killer just some sociopath?

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:50.750
Or is he a...

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.740
It was probably a witch.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.420
The wounds on the victims' bodies weren't made postmortem.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:01.120
In other words, they were sliced to pieces while they were still alive.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:07.590
There were no signs at all that they had been drugged or tied down.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.220
But there were no signs that they fought back, either.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:14.960
Or rather, maybe they never had a chance to fight back.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:19.040
In any case, it's hard to imagine that these were just ordinary murders.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:21.700
This is all hypothetical, of course.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:28.470
Anyway, let's give the place another once-over.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:31.980
Um, there's something I need to check on.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:37.420
Okay, I'll look around here a little bit more, then.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:06.650
Crows...?

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.600
I don't believe it... That girl, she...

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:28.870
Robin!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:36.670
Stop it!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.230
I'm dirty... I'm dirty... I'm dirty...

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:10.680
I'm dirty... I'm dirty...

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.010
I'm dirty... I'm dirty...

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:15.250
I'm dirty... I'm dirty...

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:17.620
I'm dirty... I'm dirty...

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:28.990
Robin!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:32.930
Robin!

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:42.940
Look out! Hide!

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:55.720
I'll never forgive you...

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:59.990
I won't let anyone soil my world!

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:05.430
Orbo can't ward off that type of power!

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:30.450
They say her family tree wasn't listed in the STN database.

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:33.150
She hadn't been flagged at all.

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:37.390
That just means that there are lots of people out there who carry the witch gene.

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:47.260
Still, you have to feel sorry for the victims.

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:50.960
They were killed just because they bothered someone who was painting.

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:57.170
Witches who exterminate humans who contaminate their world...

00:21:57.850 --> 00:22:01.370
Witch hunters who exterminate witches who contaminate the human world...

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:02.950
Huh?

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:15.720
Maybe what we're doing isn't all that different.

00:22:36.840 --> 00:22:44.830
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:47.690
Tell me.

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:59.680
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:09.570
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:14.060
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:19.430
...all those promises...

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:25.830
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:31.630
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:40.410
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
